%I A401707 #12 Nov 03 2026 12:11:51
%S A401707 1,2,3,4,5,3,7,8,9,5,11,4,13,7,5,16,17,9,19,5,21,11,23,8,25,13,27,7,
%T A401707 29,5,31,32,11,17,35,36,37,19,39,8,41,21,43,11,9,23,47,16,49,50,17,13,
%U A401707 53,27,55,8,57,29,59,5,61,31,63,64,65,11,67,17,23,35,71,9,73,37,75,19,77,39,79,16,81,41,83,21,85,43
%N A401707 The largest unitary divisor d of n with gcd(d, sigma(d)) = 1.
%C A401707 The largest term of A014567 that is a unitary divisor of n.
%C A401707 Differs from A401705 at 12, 24, 40, 45, 48, etc. See See A401704.
%H A401707 Antti Karttunen, <a href="/A401707/b401707.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%F A401707 a(n) >= A401705(n).
%F A401707 a(n) = n / A401708(n).
%e A401707 For n=12, its unitary divisors are 12, 4, 3, and 1, and the largest of these that is a term of A014567 is 4, therefore a(12) = 4.
%e A401707 For n=90, its unitary divisors are 90, 45, 18, 10, 9, 5, 2, and 1, and the largest of these that is a term of A014567 is 9, therefore a(90) = 9.
%o A401707 (PARI) A401707(n) = fordiv(n,d,if(1==gcd(d,n/d) && 1==gcd(n/d,sigma(n/d)), return(n/d)));
%Y A401707 Cf. A000203, A014567, A105402, A401708 [= n/a(n)].
%Y A401707 Cf. A401704 (k where a(k) differs from A401705(k)).
%K A401707 nonn,new
%O A401707 1,2
%A A401707 _Antti Karttunen_, Nov 03 2026
